\section{Historical Notes}
Early printers used {\it italic type} for emphasis and {\bf bold letterforms} for headings. Monospace excerpts appear as {\tt punched-card fragments} in the appendix.
Modern practice prefers command forms, but the older two-letter switches remain part of the language and appear throughout legacy manuscripts.
